- Digital 3D Brain MRI Arterial Territories Atlas, Liu et al., Scientific Data
  2023, doi:10.1038/s41597-022-01923-0. CC BY-SA 4.0.
- Juelich histological (cytoarchitectonic) atlas (Eickhoff et al.), distributed
  with FSL. NON-COMMERCIAL use.
- ICBM152 2009c nonlinear asymmetric template, Montreal Neurological Institute.

PATHOLOGY (all de-identified and de-faced at source)
- UPenn-GBM cohort, Bakas et al., Scientific Data 2022;9:453. The Cancer
  Imaging Archive. CC BY 4.0.
- UCSF-PDGM, Calabrese et al. The Cancer Imaging Archive,
  doi:10.7937/tcia.bdgf-8v37. CC BY 4.0.
- Vestibular-Schwannoma-SEG (Shapey, Kujawa et al.). The Cancer Imaging
  Archive. CC BY 4.0.
- Spine-Mets-CT-SEG. The Cancer Imaging Archive. CC BY 4.0.
- NIfTI derivatives for the TCIA glioma collections were curated via the
  Pittsburgh Fiber Data Hub (data-nih/tcia).

Only skull-stripped brain surfaces and derived lesion meshes are redistributed;
no full head or skull surface from any patient scan is included.

Several of the above are CC BY-SA: redistribution of derived model files must
preserve attribution and use compatible share-alike terms.
